#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
msgid "Ale for Two Inns"
msgstr ""

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
msgid ""
"Both inns ran dry at the same time! Six barrels for Gudrun in Vargvik and six for Orm in Hallvik. "
"With twelve crates of room, you can do it in one trip!"
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
msgid "Ale! The guests cheer. Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
msgid "At last! I thought I must serve water. Here, silver for you and for Knut."
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
msgid "Everybody drank weak ale every day: it was safer than water from the lake."
msgstr ""

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
msgid "The Sleepy Hens"
msgstr ""

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
msgid ""
"Our hens sit sleepy in the corner and lay no eggs. You are healers now: what do they need? Ask "
"Tova, and bring it."
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
msgid ""
"Sleepy hens? Lice, I bet. Dust baths with wood ash and a bit of garlic in the water. Here, take "
"garlic."
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
msgid "Garlic water, ash baths, fresh grain... Cluck! An egg! You are real healers."
msgstr ""

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
msgid "Garlic"
msgstr ""

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
msgid "the garlic"
msgstr ""

#. the thing 'the garlic' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the garlic"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
msgid "Hens bathe in dust and ash to get rid of the little bugs in their feathers."
msgstr ""

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/079_the_smiths_bellows/mission.json
msgid "The Smith's Bellows"
msgstr ""

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/079_the_smiths_bellows/mission.json
msgid ""
"My bellows burst! I need two goat hides from Sigvor in Ålberga and a pot of tar from Ekvik to make"
" new ones. My fire is cold till then!"
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/079_the_smiths_bellows/mission.json
msgid "Thick hides from my old goats. They lived long and well."
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/079_the_smiths_bellows/mission.json
msgid "Whoosh! Whoosh! The fire roars again. Take two crates of my tools."
msgstr ""

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/079_the_smiths_bellows/mission.json
msgid "Hide"
msgstr ""

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/079_the_smiths_bellows/mission.json
msgid "{count|a goat hide|{count} goat hides}"
msgstr ""

#. the thing '{count|a goat hide|{count} goat hides}' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the
#. accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same
#. as the plain translation
#: data/missions/079_the_smiths_bellows/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a goat hide|{count} goat hides}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/079_the_smiths_bellows/mission.json
msgid "Bellows of leather blew air into the forge, to make the fire hot enough for iron."
msgstr ""

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/080_grandmothers_birthday/mission.json
msgid "Grandma's Birthday"
msgstr ""

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/080_grandmothers_birthday/mission.json
msgid ""
"Psst! Your grandmother turns seventy in two days. A surprise: a new shawl from Sæunn, a cake from "
"Gudrun, and me as a guest. Do not tell her!"
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/080_grandmothers_birthday/mission.json
msgid "Blue, like her eyes. Hide it under the hay!"
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/080_grandmothers_birthday/mission.json
msgid "Honey cake with seventy almonds. I counted!"
msgstr ""

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/080_grandmothers_birthday/mission.json
msgid "A shawl? A cake? Tova? Oh, my girls... Seventy years, and this is my happiest birthday."
msgstr ""

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/080_grandmothers_birthday/mission.json
msgid "Shawl"
msgstr ""

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/080_grandmothers_birthday/mission.json
